# Commit and push without being asked

Do this after any source, script, protocol, or log change. Do not wait for the user to say "commit".

- Commit `src/`, `scripts/`, `.cursor/rules/`, `DAILY_PROGRESS.md`, `outputs/EXPERIMENT_LOG.md` and their mirrors.
- Then **`git push origin HEAD`** so a worktree wipe cannot drop unpushed commits (2026-08-16: 10 commits were only local when `src/` was deleted).
- Before submitting or changing a train/eval/QC Slurm job, commit + push the scripts and `src/` that job will load.
- After any recipe/protocol fix, commit + push immediately.

## Checkpoints (weights) — never git-add

`outputs/checkpoints/` is gitignored on purpose. Each `epoch_*.pth` is ~4.7G. GitHub rejects files that large; LFS would still dump tens of GB into the repo.

Protect weights on disk, not in git:

- Named `epoch_XXX_cancer_Y.pth` (sidecar or every-epoch saver). Never only `best.pth` / `latest.pth`.
- Record the path + val cancer in `DAILY_PROGRESS.md` / `EXPERIMENT_LOG.md` (those files *are* committed and pushed).
- Do not `git add` `*.pth`, `latest.pth`, `best.pth`, teacher-pack `*.h5`, `.env`, credentials, or `__pycache__`.
